{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1287457-exalted-tarot-stretch-goal-for-the-sidereals-book","id":1287457,"title":"Exalted Tarot - Stretch goal for the Sidereals book?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-13T01:59:09-08:00","id":1287457,"title":"Exalted Tarot - Stretch goal for the Sidereals book?","content":"I know the Sidereals Kickstarter is some distance in the future yet, but I think it would be exceptionally cool and thematically appropriate if one of the stretch goals was an Exalted Tarot deck, possibly with five elemental suits rather than the traditional four.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T05:36:07-08:00","id":1287494,"title":"","content":"This would be cool, but seems... unlikely. Fourteen cards per suit in the Minor Arcana would mean 70 cards, plus the 22 in the Major Arcana - unless basically all the art can be reused, that's a significant amount of art to buy just for a stretch goal.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Tarot is a very western-associated divinatory approach, whereas the Sidereals generally.... aren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T08:01:05-08:00","id":1287537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1287457-exalted-tarot-stretch-goal-for-the-sidereals-book?p=1287494#post1287494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be cool, but seems... unlikely. Fourteen cards per suit in the Minor Arcana would mean 70 cards, plus the 22 in the Major Arcana - unless basically all the art can be reused, that's a significant amount of art to buy just for a stretch goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one could cheat about half the total art away by having the one through ten simply display the suit symbol multiple times (just as in ordinary playing cards) rather than have art for each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T01:05:03-08:00","id":1288543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1287457-exalted-tarot-stretch-goal-for-the-sidereals-book?p=1287494#post1287494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, the Tarot is a very western-associated divinatory approach, whereas the Sidereals generally.... aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, but I don't know of any art-heavy Eastern divination techniques.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T05:52:36-08:00","id":1288581,"title":"","content":"Nothing says that you must 100% mirror what we know as the current tarot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T14:19:05-08:00","id":1288736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSly9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1287457-exalted-tarot-stretch-goal-for-the-sidereals-book?p=1288581#post1288581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing says that you must 100% mirror what we know as the current tarot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, most important step would be to come up with a setting-relevant surrogate to Tarot first then, i guess.<br /> <br /> Not to mention <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minor_Arcana\" target=\"_blank\">the suits</a> as usually given in Tarot have more in common with Fae Graces than Fate, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-16-2019, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T14:37:56-08:00","id":1288740,"title":"","content":"If it\u2019s meant to be an in-setting artifact coming up with the cards is going to depend a lot on what culture produced it. I assume if this is tied to the Sidereals, we\u2019re in theory talking about something created but a Sidereal to be used by Bureau agents in the field? In which case the suits are probably going to be based on the Maidens/Departments and incorporate the Constellations.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s a recreational deck for Dynasty the suits are probably going to be Elemental, with Dragon Cards for the Aces and Empress Cards as the highest Royal Cards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T17:11:55-08:00","id":1288784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1287457-exalted-tarot-stretch-goal-for-the-sidereals-book?p=1288740#post1288740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it\u2019s meant to be an in-setting artifact coming up with the cards is going to depend a lot on what culture produced it. I assume if this is tied to the Sidereals, we\u2019re in theory talking about something created but a Sidereal to be used by Bureau agents in the field? In which case the suits are probably going to be based on the Maidens/Departments and incorporate the Constellations.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s a recreational deck for Dynasty the suits are probably going to be Elemental, with Dragon Cards for the Aces and Empress Cards as the highest Royal Cards.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering how colorful tarot's history in itsself can be, a bit of each is possible.<br /> <br /> Once there was a game of cards, popular but one among many.<br /> Then a gambler found out by chance a ritual of divination - and its gift for thaumaturgy - while playing in a gambling house dedicated to Plentimon.<br /> This gambler would extend its stay - sometimes it lost, sometimes it won, but either way it found greater understanding and through luck, enlightnement and well-thought bluffing, opened oneself to the world of Sorcery.<br /> As thanks for its stay, miracles received and the owner's goodwill, the gambler offered to teach some of what it learned to the gambling house's croupier-priests and they accepted.<br /> This story was recorded, the card set registered and in time the lore became the stuff of legend and another point of attraction, product and service, some of the secrets of the cards spreading through rare gifted, hucksters and mystics from all directions.<br /> <br /> Just a bitch of a rambling seed of a starting tale. Sounds ok?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T19:44:16-08:00","id":1288815,"title":"","content":"A Major Arcana esque set patterned off of the Resplendent Destinies might work(in the vein of Ravenloft's Tarokka or Pathfinder's Harrow Deck).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T20:05:00-08:00","id":1288822,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m imagining right now a five suited Elemental deck that incorporates the constellations into the corresponding elemental suits (if it\u2019s the same as in previous editions, Air = Journeys, Wood = Serenity, Fire = Battles, Water = Secrets, Earth = Endings; that could always change though, one can easily see the virtue of linking Wood to Endings given the death and rebirth symbolism, or link Water and Journeys, but those are the previous associations).<br /> <br /> There is a Sixth \u201cCelestial\u201d Suit (think Major Arcana) that dates back to the First Age and is still used in Heaven, but is heretical if an Immaculate catches sight of a deck with those cards included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:10:23-08:00","id":1289770,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested in something like this. Five houses of the elements as the equivalent of the Lesser Arcana and directional beasts, and then all the sobriquets of all the Celestials as the Major Arcana. Maybe. Could be fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":""